# Streaming refactor chunk 8b — peak-RSS A/B bench
# 2026-05-18

Image: 4096×4096 RGB8, synthetic fbm-ish content (mix of structure +
randomness), distance=1.0, effort=7 (LossyConfig defaults), 4 GiB
memory budget cap.

Tool: /usr/bin/time -v (GNU time 1.9), Maximum resident set size.
3 paired runs per variant, sequential, single image / fresh process per
run.

Host: water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (16 cores, 128 GB RAM).
WSL2 Linux 6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2.
Sibling workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--streaming-chunk8b.

Build: cargo build --release --example bench_buffering_rss
Bench: ./target/release/examples/bench_buffering_rss <variant> 4096 4096 4096

Result (median of 3 runs):

  FullBuffered:    2894928 KB peak RSS  (12382528 bytes output)
  BufferedOutput:  2894432 KB peak RSS  (12382528 bytes output) — same as FullBuffered ±0.02%
  FullStreaming:   2895052 KB peak RSS  (12382528 bytes output) — same as FullBuffered ±0.01%

Bytes byte-identical across all 3 variants — confirms hash-locked
output (matches `hash_lock_features.rs` 36/36 pass).

Expected for chunk 8b: this commit lands the `XybRegionSource` trait
+ walker structure in `encode_inner` but no streaming source is wired.
The `WholeImageXybSource` `release_dc_region` is a no-op; the legacy
`drop(xyb_*)` after `compute_epf_sharpness` still drops the whole
image at once. Memory savings land in chunk 8c when a streaming
source materialises one DC group at a time + actually drops region
storage on the release hint.

xyb plane size at 4096×4096:
  padded = ceil(4096/8)*8 × ceil(4096/8)*8 = 4096×4096 pixels
  3 channels × 4096×4096 × 4 B/f32 = 192 MiB

A future chunk-8c streaming source on this size would target a peak-
RSS drop of ~192 MiB (subset of the ~2827 MiB total — the rest is
quant_field / mask1x1 / CfL map / TransformOutput / token vectors /
bitstream writer).

Reproduce:
  cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--streaming-chunk8b
  cargo build --release --example bench_buffering_rss --features 'parallel parallel-tree-learning'
  /usr/bin/time -v ./target/release/examples/bench_buffering_rss full 4096 4096 4096
  /usr/bin/time -v ./target/release/examples/bench_buffering_rss buffered 4096 4096 4096
  /usr/bin/time -v ./target/release/examples/bench_buffering_rss streaming 4096 4096 4096
